  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a YouTube video in a post to play in the app's video sheet, so that I do not have to leave the topic. Today the sheet opens but YouTube shows **« Erreur 153 – Erreur de configuration du lecteur vidéo »** with « Regarder la vidéo sur YouTube ».\n\n### Facts\n- Mac check of #499 (2026-11-10, comment 6771901895), iPad simulator iOS 27.0, build `fddb6a37`, logged out: 1 of 1 attempts; pass 2 of #499 had seen a YouTube error once.\n- The sheet loads `youtube.com/embed/…` (LOT-108, #199). Error 153 is YouTube's answer to an embed whose page it cannot identify; LOT-071 R3 sends no `Referer` to third-party hosts. The cause is **to confirm** with one request trace (no guess).\n- Vimeo in the same sheet: a removed video (`401`) leaves the sheet blank with no message (second finding, lower).\n\n### Decision needed (operator)\n- (a) send a `Referer`/`origin` identifying the app, for the YouTube player only (an exception to R3), or\n- (b) keep R3 and make « Ouvrir le lien » the way to watch, with a clear message in the sheet.\nRecommendation: (a) for the embed player host only, documented in LOT-071's spec.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A public YouTube video plays in the sheet (or the chosen fallback shows a clear message).\n- [ ] An unavailable Vimeo/YouTube video shows a message, never a blank sheet.\n- [ ] Mac check on a device.\n\nRefs #499, #465, LOT-108 (#199), LOT-071.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
